    "fullDescription": "The scheme, administered by the Department for the Welfare of Differently Abled & Senior Citizens (A.P. Differently Abled & Senior Citizens Assistance Corporation), proposes to procure 200 laptops at ₹30,000 each for eligible students of Andhra Pradesh. Benefits are tiered by parent/guardian income: Category I (income ≤ ₹15,000 / month) – full cost covered; Category II (₹15,000‑₹20,000 / month) – half cost covered; Category III (income > ₹20,000 / month) – beneficiary pays full cost. Eligibility requires the student to be a native of Andhra Pradesh, have a visual, hearing, speech or orthopedic disability, and be enrolled in postgraduate or professional courses. The laptop is sanctioned only once in the beneficiary’s lifetime. Applications are submitted online via the official website, with a multi‑step registration and form‑filling process. Required documents include a bonafide certificate, parents’ income certificate, disability certificate, Aadhaar card, and mobile number.",
